;;; Syntax probe — is-a-shapes.
;;;
;;; The kernel `is-a` head with each argument kind it can hold in the subject
;;; position: a name, and digits, which are a name (M1f S1f.5.4's name rule).
;;; The variable and the wildcard it carried until M1f S1f.5.5's swap are
;;; refused at the parse (S1f.5.2's G-6 and S1f.5.1), Q-M1f.2 (a)'s rewrite.
;;;
;;; One of the eighteen node-kind fixtures. As corpus entries they are
;;; rendered under every parse view and every op, and each rendering is
;;; digested by `corpus_shapes.md5`, so a change to how any of these
;;; shapes is drawn moves a digest. They exist because no *puzzle*
;;; contains these shapes.

(is-a a T)
(is-a 7 T)
